---
---
<section class="py-20 border-t border-gray-200/50 relative z-10 px-6 max-w-4xl mx-auto w-full">
  <div class="text-center mb-16">
    <h2 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-tertiary mb-3">FAQ</h2>
    <h3 class="text-heading-32 sm:text-heading-40 font-bold text-gray-1000 tracking-tight">
      Frequently Asked Questions
    </h3>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-4">
    <!-- FAQ 1 -->
    <details class="group border border-gray-200 rounded-sm bg-background-200 p-6 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
      <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-1.5 focus-visible:outline-none rounded-sm">
        <h4 class="text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-gray-1000">
          Is my identity really 100% anonymous?
        </h4>
        <span class="relative h-5 w-5 shrink-0">
          <svg class="absolute inset-0 h-5 w-5 opacity-100 group-open:opacity-0 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 9v6m3-3H9m12 0a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
          </svg>
          <svg class="absolute inset-0 h-5 w-5 opacity-0 group-open:opacity-100 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 12H9m12 0a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
          </svg>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <p class="mt-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed border-t border-gray-200/50 pt-4">
        Yes. Peerly does not store your name, student ID, or university email. Your email is processed only to confirm student status, and a secure cryptographic hash is created for rate-limiting, after which the email address is discarded immediately.
      </p>
    </details>

    <!-- FAQ 2 -->
    <details class="group border border-gray-200 rounded-sm bg-background-200 p-6 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
      <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-1.5 focus-visible:outline-none rounded-sm">
        <h4 class="text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-gray-1000">
          Who are the Peer Mentors?
        </h4>
        <span class="relative h-5 w-5 shrink-0">
          <svg class="absolute inset-0 h-5 w-5 opacity-100 group-open:opacity-0 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 9v6m3-3H9m12 0a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
          </svg>
          <svg class="absolute inset-0 h-5 w-5 opacity-0 group-open:opacity-100 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 12H9m12 0a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
          </svg>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <p class="mt-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed border-t border-gray-200/50 pt-4">
        Peer Mentors are trained upper-year students who have been verified by university administration. They receive training in active listening, empathy, boundaries, and crisis escalation protocols.
      </p>
    </details>

    <!-- FAQ 3 -->
    <details class="group border border-gray-200 rounded-sm bg-background-200 p-6 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
      <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-1.5 focus-visible:outline-none rounded-sm">
        <h4 class="text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-gray-1000">
          What happens in a crisis situation?
        </h4>
        <span class="relative h-5 w-5 shrink-0">
          <svg class="absolute inset-0 h-5 w-5 opacity-100 group-open:opacity-0 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 9v6m3-3H9m12 0a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
          </svg>
          <svg class="absolute inset-0 h-5 w-5 opacity-0 group-open:opacity-100 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 12H9m12 0a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
          </svg>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <p class="mt-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed border-t border-gray-200/50 pt-4">
        Peerly is not a crisis treatment center. If a student is in danger, peer mentors follow a strict escalation protocol, sharing links to immediate clinical help, crisis phone lines, or counseling services.
      </p>
    </details>

    <!-- FAQ 4 -->
    <details class="group border border-gray-200 rounded-sm bg-background-200 p-6 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
      <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-1.5 focus-visible:outline-none rounded-sm">
        <h4 class="text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-gray-1000">
          How do administrators manage the platform?
        </h4>
        <span class="relative h-5 w-5 shrink-0">
          <svg class="absolute inset-0 h-5 w-5 opacity-100 group-open:opacity-0 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 9v6m3-3H9m12 0a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
          </svg>
          <svg class="absolute inset-0 h-5 w-5 opacity-0 group-open:opacity-100 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 12H9m12 0a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
          </svg>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <p class="mt-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed border-t border-gray-200/50 pt-4">
        Through the secure Admin Dashboard, designated staff can view aggregated usage statistics, verify new peer mentors, publish platform-wide announcements, audit reported posts/messages, and manage mental health guides.
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
